From: Anton Argirov <anton.argirov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:22:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(neogs): emulate the SD slot and load NeoGS firmware

Run the external NeoGS flash image on the General Sound Z80 with
NeoGS memory and port decoding. Model its independent SPI bus and
support raw read/write media, including the single-block transfers
used by Wild Commander and the multiple-block transfers used by ERS.

Expose the firmware and SD image in the SD/MMC menu and in startup
options. Add ZRCP insert/eject commands for repeatable media tests.
Expose card detect and write protect through SSTAT.

Advance NeoGS up to the Spectrum bus timestamp before every mailbox
access. Wild Commander reads the data flag immediately after sending
the last request byte; running NeoGS only at the end of a scanline
can let the host clear that flag before NeoGS consumes the byte.

